<%# respond_to? guard: bsdports gates the social routes behind BSDPORTS_SOCIAL=1,
    so notifications_path is undefined there and every signed-in page raised.

    No class default. The one that stood here was "nav-link", which no stylesheet
    in any of the three apps defines — the tree spells the nav class nav_link,
    with an underscore — so the attribute reached no rule and the link has always
    painted as the bare anchor its three siblings in bsdports' nav are. Naming
    the real class would change what is painted and belongs to the operator; the
    hook that promises styling it does not have is what goes.

    The label is a key, not a word: these apps default to Norwegian and the link
    pointed at notifications while reading "Inbox" in every locale. %>
<% if authenticated? && respond_to?(:notifications_path) %>
  <%= link_to t("nav.notifications"), notifications_path, class: local_assigns[:class_name] %>
<% end %>
